# Half-car test rig, HMMWV rear axle: sprung mass free to heave and roll,
# left and right double-wishbone corners, and independent shaker posts under
# each wheel as the vertical position drivers. Hardpoints, masses, and
# inertias are the HMMWV rear suspension data shipped with Project Chrono
# (data/vehicle/hmmwv/): suspension HMMWV_DoubleWishboneRear.json, chassis
# 2086.52 kg (halved), wheel 18.8 kg + tire 37.6 kg per corner, tire radius
# 0.467 -- same wheel/tire/control-arm parts as the front (quartercar.mech),
# only the rear-specific hardpoints, upright, and spring/shock curves differ.
# The rear is used (rather than the front) because its "tierod" is grounded
# on the chassis at both ends -- no steering rack -- so it is an ordinary
# fixed-length link with no actuation to model, unlike the front's tie rod.
#
# Axes are ISO vehicle: x forward, y outboard-left, z up. The base frame
# sits on the VEHICLE CENTERLINE at the DESIGN WHEEL-CENTER HEIGHT and the
# rear axle's x station (Chrono's rear suspension hardpoints, which are
# already centerline-relative in y, minus the wheel-center x/z offset
# (0.036, -, -0.026): the rear Spindle COM in HMMWV_DoubleWishboneRear.json).
# Left-side hardpoints are used as given; right-side hardpoints are the
# mirror image (negate y), exactly how Chrono's own template mirrors one
# side's JSON to build the other. Every loop closes at q = 0 with both
# spindles at identity quaternion.
#
# Topology (tree DOF 20, nc 16, mobility 4):
#   0 chassis_heave  prismatic z   massless-ish carrier body: exists only so
#                                  heave and roll can be two chained
#                                  single-DOF joints (this format has no
#                                  combined 2-DOF joint). Real inertia is
#                                  ~zero and lives entirely on body 1 --
#                                  same pattern as elbow.mech's wrist chain.
#   1 chassis_roll   revolute x    the actual sprung half-mass: half the full
#                                  HMMWV chassis mass and roll/pitch/yaw
#                                  inertia (HMMWV_Chassis.json), on the
#                                  assumption the front/rear split is even.
#                                  Wishbones and the anti-roll "tierod" link
#                                  hang off this body, matching quartercar's
#                                  chassis (there the single sprung body took
#                                  that role).
#   2 LCA_L          revolute x    left lower control arm; Chrono's pivot
#                                  axis is exactly x (front/back pivots both
#                                  at y=0.307, z=0)
#   3 UCA_L          revolute x    left upper control arm; real pivot axis
#                                  skewed a few deg from x, idealized to x
#                                  (as in quartercar) since tree joints are
#                                  axis-aligned; pivot at the front/back
#                                  midpoint
#   4 spindle_L      floating      left upright + spindle + wheel + tire
#                                  lumped (no wheel-spin DOF), positioned by
#                                  the loop joints below; frame at the wheel
#                                  center
#   5 post_L         prismatic z   left shaker pad at the contact patch: a
#                                  POSITION DRIVER. Drive q[.] through its
#                                  own tau slot (e.g. a stiff PD servo
#                                  tracking a road/post profile)
#   6 LCA_R          revolute x    right lower control arm, mirror of body 2
#   7 UCA_R          revolute x    right upper control arm, mirror of body 3
#   8 spindle_R      floating      right corner, mirror of body 4
#   9 post_R         prismatic z   right shaker pad, mirror of body 5
#
# Loop joints (each spindle has ball joints everywhere, so like quartercar
# it is a floating body pinned by constraints -- spherical tree joints
# aren't implemented), 4 per side:
#   spherical  LCA outer ball  -> spindle lower ball
#   spherical  UCA outer ball  -> spindle upper ball
#   distance   "tierod" rod, chassis_roll -> spindle steering-arm point
#              (Chrono's rear Tierod hardpoints -- grounded on the chassis
#              at both ends since the rear doesn't steer); kills the
#              leftover spin about the kingpin axis
#   distance   driver rod, post pad -> wheel center, length = tire radius:
#              a rigid "tire" with balls at patch and hub, exactly as in
#              quartercar
#
# Mobility 4 = chassis heave + chassis roll + post_L position + post_R
# position. Left/right suspension deflection is the difference between
# chassis motion (heave, and roll times half-track) and each post. Tire
# loads apply via fext on the spindles.
#
# The real HMMWV rear coil spring and shock (data/vehicle/hmmwv/suspension/
# HMMWV_DoubleWishboneRear.json) are modeled as two TSDAs per side, sharing
# the LCA mount point but not the chassis mount point, same as quartercar.
# Unlike quartercar, both TSDA anchors here are attached to the body that
# physically carries them (chassis_roll for the upper mount, the LCA for the
# lower) rather than the fixed base -- with a roll DOF present, an anchor
# pinned to the fixed base would pick up a spurious length change from pure
# heave/roll instead of only the wishbone's rotation relative to the
# chassis, which is what a real spring mounted between chassis and arm
# actually measures.
# Coordinates converted to this file's base/LCA frames the same way as
# quartercar (Chrono chassis-relative point minus the wheel-center x/z
# offset (0.036, -0.026); the LCA-frame point additionally minus the LCA
# pivot (0, 0.307, 0) in that same Chrono frame; mirror y for the right
# side):
#   spring: chassis (-0.104, 0.502, 0.256) -> chassis_roll (-0.140, +-0.502, 0.282)
#           arm     (-0.097, 0.543, -0.047) -> LCA (-0.097, +-0.236, -0.047)
#   shock:  chassis (-0.104, 0.498, 0.323) -> chassis_roll (-0.140, +-0.498, 0.349)
#           arm     (-0.097, 0.544, -0.038) -> LCA (-0.097, +-0.237, -0.038)
# The JSON spring is a nonlinear curve (progressive, free length 0.382 m);
# this format only has a linear TSDA, so k is the curve's slope at zero
# deflection (8020.869 N / 0.02 m). The shock's damping coefficient is
# already linear and used directly. Both are passive (no 'input').
#
# q layout (nq 22, nv 20): q[0] chassis_heave, q[1] chassis_roll,
# q[2] LCA_L, q[3] UCA_L, q[4..10] spindle_L quaternion + position,
# q[11] post_L, q[12] LCA_R, q[13] UCA_R, q[14..20] spindle_R quaternion +
# position, q[21] post_R. Design pose: q = 0 with q[4] = q[14] = 1.

gravity 0 0 -9.81
stab 0.05

body                     # 0: chassis_heave, carrier for the heave DOF (see header)
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 0 0 0
mass 1
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.01 0.01 0.01 0 0 0

body                     # 1: chassis_roll, half the HMMWV sprung mass, free heave+roll
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 0 0 0
mass 1043.26
cg 0 0 0.283             # vehicle centerline, HMMWV CG height (~0.75 above ground)
inertia 539.26 1477.83 1785.10 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 2: left lower control arm, pivot y=0.307 z=0 (Chrono, exact x axis)
parent 1
joint revolute x
tree -0.036 0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 3: left upper control arm, pivot at front/back midpoint
parent 1
joint revolute x
tree 0.177 0.462 0.252
mass 5.813
cg -0.089 0.127 -0.005
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 4: left spindle assembly (upright + spindle + wheel + tire),
parent -1                #    frame at the wheel center
joint floating
tree 0 0.910 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 -0.0342 0            # upright CG sits 0.159 inboard of the wheel center
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 5: left shaker post pad at the contact patch -- a driver
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 0 0.910 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

body                     # 6: right lower control arm, mirror of body 2
parent 1
joint revolute x
tree -0.036 -0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 -0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 7: right upper control arm, mirror of body 3
parent 1
joint revolute x
tree 0.177 -0.462 0.252
mass 5.813
cg -0.089 -0.127 -0.005
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 8: right spindle assembly, mirror of body 4
parent -1
joint floating
tree 0 -0.910 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 0.0342 0             # upright CG sits 0.159 inboard of the wheel center
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 9: right shaker post pad, mirror of body 5
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 0 -0.910 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

loop                     # left lower ball joint: LCA_L outer end to spindle_L
predecessor 2
successor 4
joint spherical
ptree 0.036 0.480 -0.118
stree 0 -0.123 -0.092

loop                     # left upper ball joint: UCA_L outer end to spindle_L
predecessor 3
successor 4
joint spherical
ptree -0.177 0.254 -0.010
stree 0 -0.194 0.242

loop                     # left tierod: chassis_roll to the spindle_L steering-arm point
predecessor 1
successor 4
joint distance
ptree 0.187 0.416 0.085
stree 0.134 -0.089 0.017
length 0.4140749

loop                     # left driver rod: post_L pad to wheel center, one tire radius
predecessor 5
successor 4
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

loop                     # right lower ball joint: LCA_R outer end to spindle_R
predecessor 6
successor 8
joint spherical
ptree 0.036 -0.480 -0.118
stree 0 0.123 -0.092

loop                     # right upper ball joint: UCA_R outer end to spindle_R
predecessor 7
successor 8
joint spherical
ptree -0.177 -0.254 -0.010
stree 0 0.194 0.242

loop                     # right tierod: chassis_roll to the spindle_R steering-arm point
predecessor 1
successor 8
joint distance
ptree 0.187 -0.416 0.085
stree 0.134 0.089 0.017
length 0.4140749

loop                     # right driver rod: post_R pad to wheel center, one tire radius
predecessor 9
successor 8
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

poi springChassis_L 1 -0.140 0.502 0.282
poi springArm_L 2 -0.097 0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_L 1 -0.140 0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_L 2 -0.097 0.237 -0.038

poi springChassis_R 1 -0.140 -0.502 0.282
poi springArm_R 6 -0.097 -0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_R 1 -0.140 -0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_R 6 -0.097 -0.237 -0.038

tsda spring_L               # HMMWV rear coil spring, linearized (see header)
from springChassis_L
to springArm_L
k 401043.45
c 0
l0 0.382

tsda shock_L                # HMMWV rear shock absorber
from shockChassis_L
to shockArm_L
k 0
c 36725.2201
l0 0.382

tsda spring_R               # mirror of spring_L
from springChassis_R
to springArm_R
k 401043.45
c 0
l0 0.382

tsda shock_R                 # mirror of shock_L
from shockChassis_R
to shockArm_R
k 0
c 36725.2201
l0 0.382
